<Layout title="Privacy — Reelkeep" description="How Reelkeep handles submitted links, temporary videos and request limits."><article class="document"><p class="eyebrow">THE SMALL PRINT, KEPT SIMPLE</p><h1>Privacy.</h1><p>Last updated 28 October 2026.</p><h2>What the app processes</h2><p>Your submitted Instagram link goes to the configured backend so it can request publicly accessible video information. The backend processes your network address to enforce request limits. It holds a one-way hash in memory for up to an hour; it does not store a link history, Instagram passwords, browser sessions or account cookies.</p><h2>Temporary videos</h2><p>Successful videos are stored temporarily for about ten minutes, with brief extensions for active downloads. Files are cleaned periodically and on orderly shutdown. A restart or idle suspension may delete them sooner. Each video is accessed with a random link; anyone with that link can access it until it expires. Videos you save remain on your own device.</p><h2>Third parties</h2><p>The frontend host and backend host process network requests and may retain infrastructure logs according to their own policies. Instagram receives the backend’s source requests. The application does not add analytics, advertising trackers or marketing cookies. Clipboard content is read only when you press Paste and your browser permits it.</p><h2>Your choices</h2><p>Use the tool only for content you may download. Avoid sharing temporary video links. If you do not want a link processed, do not submit it. This prototype has no user accounts or personal-data dashboard.</p><p><a href="/">Return to the downloader</a></p></article></Layout>
